## 2. Methodology
- Automated testing: axe-core, Lighthouse
- Manual testing: Keyboard navigation, Screen readers (NVDA, VoiceOver)
- Tools: WAVE, Color Contrast Analyser, Accessibility Insights

## 3. Summary of Findings

| WCAG Principle | Guideline | Pass | Fail | N/A | Total |
|----------------|-----------|------|------|-----|-------|
| Perceivable | 1.1 - 1.4 | 12 | 3 | 2 | 17 |
| Operable | 2.1 - 2.5 | 15 | 2 | 1 | 18 |
| Understandable | 3.1 - 3.3 | 8 | 1 | 2 | 11 |
| Robust | 4.1 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 5 |
| **Total** | | **40** | **6** | **5** | **51** |

## 4. Detailed Findings

### Critical (Must Fix - Blocks Access)
| ID | Component | WCAG | Issue | Impact | Recommendation |
|----|-----------|------|-------|--------|----------------|
| A11Y-001 | Checkout Form | 1.3.1 | Form labels not programmatically associated | Screen reader users cannot identify fields | Add `<label for="id">` or `aria-label` |
| A11Y-002 | Modal Dialog | 2.4.3 | Focus not trapped in modal | Keyboard users can tab outside modal | Implement focus trap |
| A11Y-003 | Color Status | 1.4.1 | Error states use color only | Colorblind users cannot distinguish | Add icons/text indicators |

### High (Should Fix - Significant Barrier)
| ID | Component | WCAG | Issue | Impact | Recommendation |
|----|-----------|------|-------|--------|----------------|
| A11Y-004 | Navigation | 2.4.7 | Focus indicator missing on custom buttons | Keyboard users lose focus visibility | Add visible focus styles |
| A11Y-005 | Data Table | 1.3.1 | Table headers not associated with cells | Screen reader users cannot understand data | Use `<th scope="col">` |

### Medium (Should Fix - Moderate Barrier)
| ID | Component | WCAG | Issue | Impact | Recommendation |
|----|-----------|------|-------|--------|----------------|
| A11Y-006 | Carousel | 2.2.2 | Auto-advancing carousel cannot be paused | Users with cognitive disabilities cannot read content | Add pause/play controls |

